.IX Title "Lucy::Document::Doc 3pm"
.TH Lucy::Document::Doc 3pm 2026-09-16 "perl v5.40.1" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
Lucy::Document::Doc \- A document.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 4
\&    my $doc = Lucy::Document::Doc\->new(
\&        fields => { foo => \*(Aqfoo foo\*(Aq, bar => \*(Aqbar bar\*(Aq },
\&    );
\&    $indexer\->add_doc($doc);
.Ve
.PP
Doc objects allow access to field values via hashref overloading:
.PP
.Vb 2
\&    $doc\->{foo} = \*(Aqnew value for field "foo"\*(Aq;
\&    print "foo: $doc\->{foo}\en";
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
A Doc object is akin to a row in a database, in that it is made up of one
or more fields, each of which has a value.
.SH CONSTRUCTORS
.IX Header "CONSTRUCTORS"
.SS new
.IX Subsection "new"
.Vb 3
\&    my $doc = Lucy::Document::Doc\->new(
\&        fields => { foo => \*(Aqfoo foo\*(Aq, bar => \*(Aqbar bar\*(Aq },
\&    );
.Ve
.PP
Create a new Document.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBfields\fR \- Field-value pairs.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBdoc_id\fR \- Internal Lucy document id.  Default of 0 (an
invalid doc id).
.SH METHODS
.IX Header "METHODS"
.SS set_doc_id
.IX Subsection "set_doc_id"
.Vb 1
\&    $doc\->set_doc_id($doc_id);
.Ve
.PP
Set internal Lucy document id.
.SS get_doc_id
.IX Subsection "get_doc_id"
.Vb 1
\&    my $int = $doc\->get_doc_id();
.Ve
.PP
Retrieve internal Lucy document id.
.SS store
.IX Subsection "store"
.Vb 1
\&    $doc\->store($field, $value);
.Ve
.PP
Store a field value in the Doc.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBfield\fR \- The field name.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBvalue\fR \- The value.
.SS get_fields
.IX Subsection "get_fields"
.Vb 1
\&    my $hashref = $doc\->get_fields();
.Ve
.PP
Return the Doc's backing fields hash.
.SS get_size
.IX Subsection "get_size"
.Vb 1
\&    my $int = $doc\->get_size();
.Ve
.PP
Return the number of fields in the Doc.
.SS extract
.IX Subsection "extract"
.Vb 1
\&    my $obj = $doc\->extract($field);
.Ve
.PP
Retrieve the field’s value, or NULL if the field is not present.
.SS field_names
.IX Subsection "field_names"
.Vb 1
\&    my $arrayref = $doc\->field_names();
.Ve
.PP
Return a list of names of all fields present.
.SH INHERITANCE
.IX Header "INHERITANCE"
Lucy::Document::Doc isa Clownfish::Obj.
